  "category" : "Students and Teachers",
  "createdAt" : 1706290996,
  "description" : "This dataset contains data about Massachusetts public school teachers and their qualifications by subject since 2008, including the count of teacher full time equivalents (FTE), the ratio of students to teachers, teacher experience, and credentials.\n\nUnder Massachusetts state law, Commonwealth charter schools have different educator qualification requirements than traditional public schools and generally, as a matter of state law, are not required to be licensed. See the <a href=\"http://www.doe.mass.edu/charter/guidance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Educator Qualifications in Commonwealth Charter Schools</a> technical advisory for more information.\n\nIn 2025 and earlier, unusually high student/teacher ratios were sometimes calculated for teacher FTEs between 0.0 and 0.1.\n\nThis dataset contains the same data that is also published on our DESE Profiles site: \n<a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/teacherdata.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Teacher Data Report</a>\n\n<b>List of Subjects</b><ul><li>All Teachers</li><li>Arts</li><li>Civics/Government</li><li>Core-All Subjects</li><li>Economics</li><li>English/Language Arts</li><li>Foreign Language</li><li>Geography</li><li>History</li><li>Mathematics</li><li>Reading</li><li>Science</li><li>Social Studies/Social Sciences</li></ul>",
